.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKV-LIST-TABLES 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekv-list-tables \- list the account's tables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekv list-tables
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR \fIFIELD\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-direction\fR \fIasc\fR|\fIdesc\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the tables of the account you are logged in to, each with its
key, its ERN and how many items it holds.
.PP
Each count is a count, so a listing of many tables costs one query per
table. On an installation with a great many of them, ask for a page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fITEXT\fR
Only tables whose name starts with this.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Most to return. Without it, all of them.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page, applied when a page size is given.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-column " " \fIFIELD\fR
Field to sort by. Defaults to the name.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-direction " " \fIasc\fR|\fIdesc\fR
Which way to sort. Defaults to ascending.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing is printed, with the account's total table count.
.TP
.B 1
The request could not be sent or was rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ekv list-tables
euclid-cli ekv list-tables --prefix supplier --page-size 20
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekv (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-describe-table (1)
